# PetelAssistants Guidelines

Before making any changes under `PetelAssistants/`, read `.github/instructions/petelassistants.instructions.md`.

For year-scoped UI (dashboard → year hub → assistants / entitlements), see `PetelAssistants/docs/year-management-screens.md`.

## Security — Required API Endpoints

The shared Blazor stack (`Petel.BlazorCore`) calls these endpoints on startup or on every action. If any are missing the frontend degrades silently.

### `SessionController` (all 5 required)
| Endpoint | Why it is required |
|---|---|
| `GET  session/timeout-config` | `SessionTimeoutService.InitializeAsync()` — returns `{ timeoutMinutes, warningMinutes }` from `IAttributeCache("Security_SessionTimeoutMinutes")` + `SecuritySettings` fallback. **Missing → client defaults to 10 min, not the DB value.** |
| `GET  session/properties` | Debug modal in `MainLayout.razor` |
| `DELETE session/property/{key}` | Session property cleanup |
| `GET  session` | Already present |
| `POST session/property` | Already present |

### `SecurityController` (all 5 required)
| Endpoint | `ActionAuthorizationService` method |
|---|---|
| `GET  security/user-actions` | `GetUserAllowedActionIds(userId, entityId)` |
| `POST security/verify-onclick` | `VerifyActionByNameAsync(…, "ONCLICK_BUTTON", screenName)` — `FunctionName` is the action name |
| `POST security/verify-menu` | `VerifyActionByNameAsync(…, "MENU_NAVIGATION", "")` — `MenuItemName` is the action name |
| `POST security/verify-action` | `VerifyUserActionAccessAsync(userId, entityId, actionId)` |
| `POST security/verify-action-secure` | Full audit log path — already present |

### `AuthController` (both required)
| Endpoint | What it does |
|---|---|
| `POST auth/logout` | Reads `Authorization: Bearer` header, calls `InvalidateSession(token)` |
| `GET  auth/check` | Returns `{ isAuthenticated, user }` from `GetUserSession(token)` |

## Session Timeout — How It Works

- **Blazor client** (`SessionTimeoutService`): calls `GET session/timeout-config` on init → uses `timeoutMinutes` returned. Falls back to **10 min** hardcoded default if the endpoint is unreachable.
- **API server** (`UserSessionService.IsSessionValid`): re-reads `IAttributeCache("Security_SessionTimeoutMinutes")` on every session check → correctly uses DB value after startup.
- **JWT expiry** (`JwtTokenService`): reads `JWT_ExpirationHours` from the attribute cache **once at construction**, which occurs before `SystemAttributeLoaderHostedService` runs → always uses `appsettings.json` `Security:Jwt:ExpirationHours` (default 8 h). This is a known limitation.

## `SessionController` — Inject `IAttributeCache` for `timeout-config`

```csharp
public SessionController(
    UserSessionService userSessionService,
    IAttributeCache attributeCache,           // ← required for timeout-config
    IOptions<SecuritySettings> securitySettings,
    ILogger<SessionController> logger)
    : base(userSessionService, logger) { … }
```